IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cra-types`

-- Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK) — GOALS 1 AND 2: GOODS (ss 19(14)-(15),
-- 20(15), 22, 24).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2015-15.txt.

§ `Goals 1 and 2 — goods`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 22(3), 24(11): the day on which "these have all happened" — transfer,
-- delivery and (if required) the installation notice.
@ref ss 22(3), 24(11)
GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the last of the events happened for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g's `installation notified on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN both
    WHEN JUST i  THEN `the later of` both i
    WHERE
        both MEANS `the later of` (g's `ownership or possession transferred on`) (g's `delivered on`)

§§ `Goal 1 — the short-term right to reject (s 22)`

-- s 22(3) "the end of 30 days beginning with the first day after these have
-- all happened". (4): perishable goods, the end of the shorter period.
@ref s 22(3)-(4)
GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`
GIVETH A DATE
`the original time limit for the short-term right to reject for` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g's `perishes by`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN thirty
    WHEN JUST p  THEN `the earlier of` thirty p
    WHERE
        thirty MEANS `the day` 30 `days after` (`the day the last of the events happened for` g)

-- s 22(6) "If the consumer requests or agrees to the repair or replacement of
-- goods, the period ... stops running for the length of the waiting period."
-- (8) the waiting period begins with the request day and ends with the day
-- the goods are received. (7) "If goods supplied ... do not conform ..., the
-- time limit ... is then either— (a) 7 days after the waiting period ends,
-- or (b) if later, the original time limit ..., extended by the waiting
-- period."
@ref s 22(1)-(8)
@export The last day to exercise the short-term right to reject under s 22 of the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK): the end of 30 days beginning with the day after transfer, delivery and any installation notice (or a shorter period for perishable goods), extended by the length of any repair or replacement waiting period; if the goods supplied after it still do not conform, the later of 7 days after the waiting period ends and that extended limit. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`                       @desc The dates of transfer, delivery, any installation notice, and any perishability limit
      r IS A MAYBE `Repair or replacement`        @desc Any repair or replacement: when requested and received, and whether the goods still do not conform
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the short-term right to reject for` g `with` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN NOTHING THEN original
    WHEN JUST w  THEN
        IF   w's `requested or agreed on` GREATER THAN original
        THEN original
        ELSE IF   w's `still do not conform`
             THEN `the later of` (`the day` 7 `days after` (w's `goods received back on`)) (extended w)
             ELSE extended w
    WHERE
        original MEANS `the original time limit for the short-term right to reject for` g
        GIVEN w IS A `Repair or replacement`
        GIVETH A DATE
        extended w MEANS
            `the day` (Day (w's `goods received back on`) MINUS Day (w's `requested or agreed on`) PLUS 1) `days after` original

§§ `Goal 2 — the presumption, and the final right to reject`

-- s 19(14) "goods which do not conform to the contract at any time within
-- the period of six months beginning with the day on which the goods were
-- delivered to the consumer must be taken not to have conformed to it on that
-- day." (15): not if it is established they did conform, or the presumption
-- is incompatible with the nature of the goods or of the non-conformity.
@ref s 19(14)-(15)
@export Whether goods are taken not to have conformed to the contract on delivery under s 19(14) of the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK): the non-conformity appeared within the six months beginning with the day of delivery, unless it is established they conformed on that day or the presumption is incompatible with the goods or the fault. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`  @desc The day of delivery
      f IS A `Fault facts`   @desc When the fault appeared, and whether conformity on delivery is established or the presumption incompatible
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods are presumed not to have conformed on delivery for` g `with` f IF
        f's `fault appeared on` AT MOST `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (g's `delivered on`)
    AND f's `fault appeared on` AT LEAST g's `delivered on`
    AND NOT (f's `established to conform on delivery`)
    AND NOT (f's `presumption incompatible with the goods or the fault`)

-- s 24(5) "A consumer who has the right to a price reduction and the final
-- right to reject may only exercise one (not both), and may only do so in
-- one of these situations— (a) after one repair or one replacement, the goods
-- do not conform ...; (b) because of section 23(3) the consumer can require
-- neither repair nor replacement ...; or (c) the consumer has required the
-- trader to repair or replace the goods, but the trader is in breach of the
-- requirement ... to do so within a reasonable time and without significant
-- inconvenience".
@ref s 24(5)
@export Whether the final right to reject or a price reduction is available under s 24(5) of the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK): after one repair or replacement the goods still do not conform, neither repair nor replacement can be required, or the trader failed to repair or replace within a reasonable time. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN t IS A `Tier two facts`  @desc Which of the s 24(5) situations has arisen
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tier-two remedies are available under` t IF
        t's `after one repair or replacement the goods still do not conform`
    OR  t's `neither repair nor replacement can be required`
    OR  t's `the trader failed to repair or replace within a reasonable time`

-- s 24(8) "any refund ... may be reduced by a deduction for use"; (10) "No
-- deduction may be made if the final right to reject is exercised in the
-- first 6 months ..., unless— (a) the goods consist of a motor vehicle, or
-- (b) [specified goods]." (11): the first 6 months begin with the first day
-- after the events.
@ref s 24(8)-(11)
@export The refund on exercising the final right to reject under s 24 of the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK): the price paid, less the deduction for use claimed, except that no deduction is made if the right is exercised in the first 6 months (beginning with the day after transfer, delivery and any installation notice) unless the goods are a motor vehicle or specified goods; 0 if the final right is not available under s 24(5). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods supply`     @desc The dates of transfer, delivery and any installation notice
      t IS A `Tier two facts`   @desc The s 24(5) situation, the price, the deduction claimed, the goods, and when the right was exercised
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund on final rejection for` g `with` t MEANS
    IF   NOT (`the tier-two remedies are available under` t)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   inFirstSixMonths AND NOT (t's `a motor vehicle or specified goods`)
         THEN t's `price paid`
         ELSE IF   t's `deduction for use claimed` AT MOST t's `price paid`
              THEN t's `price paid` MINUS t's `deduction for use claimed`
              ELSE 0
    WHERE
        inFirstSixMonths MEANS
            t's `final right exercised on` AT MOST `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` (`the day` 1 `days after` (`the day the last of the events happened for` g))

-- s 20(15) "A refund ... must be given without undue delay, and in any event
-- within 14 days beginning with the day on which the trader agrees that the
-- consumer is entitled to a refund." The last day is that day + 13.
@ref ss 20(15), 56(4)
@export The last day for a trader to give a refund under s 20(15) or s 56(4) of the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK): within the 14 days beginning with the day the trader agrees the consumer is entitled (that day + 13). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN agreed IS A DATE  @desc The day the trader agreed the consumer is entitled to a refund
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for a refund agreed on` agreed MEANS
    `the day` 13 `days after` agreed
